### fieldapply example requests (REST Client / IntelliJ / VS Code style)
### Replace {{base}} if your port differs.

@base = http://localhost:8080

### health
GET {{base}}/healthz

### create a resource with collection semantics
POST {{base}}/v1/resources
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "app",
  "manager": "platform",
  "body": {
    "spec": {
      "replicas": 3,
      "tags": ["x", "y"],
      "containers": [
        {"name": "web", "image": "web:1", "port": 8080},
        {"name": "worker", "image": "worker:1"}
      ]
    }
  },
  "schema": {
    "lists": {".spec.tags": "set", ".spec.containers": "keyed"},
    "keys": {".spec.containers": "name"}
  }
}

### autoscaler adopts replicas at the current value (shares the leaf)
POST {{base}}/v1/resources/app/apply
Content-Type: application/json

{"manager": "autoscaler", "body": {"spec": {"replicas": 3}}}

### autoscaler force-scales (platform still holds a share)
POST {{base}}/v1/resources/app/apply
Content-Type: application/json

{"manager": "autoscaler", "force": true, "reason": "scale-up",
 "body": {"spec": {"replicas": 7}}}

### platform stale write -> 409 naming autoscaler
POST {{base}}/v1/resources/app/apply
Content-Type: application/json

{"manager": "platform", "body": {"spec": {"replicas": 11}}}

### netpol adds a set element
POST {{base}}/v1/resources/app/apply
Content-Type: application/json

{"manager": "netpol", "body": {"spec": {"tags": ["z"]}}}

### netpol force-takes one leaf of a keyed-list element
POST {{base}}/v1/resources/app/apply
Content-Type: application/json

{"manager": "netpol", "force": true,
 "body": {"spec": {"containers": [{"name": "web", "port": 9090}]}}}

### platform deletes the worker element; carries current foreign values
POST {{base}}/v1/resources/app/apply
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "manager": "platform",
  "body": {"spec": {"replicas": 7, "tags": ["x", "y"],
    "containers": [{"name": "web", "image": "web:1", "port": 9090}]}}
}

### optimistic concurrency: stale baseRevision -> 409 revision_stale
POST {{base}}/v1/resources/app/apply
Content-Type: application/json

{"manager": "platform", "baseRevision": 1, "body": {"spec": {"replicas": 7}}}

### read live state
GET {{base}}/v1/resources/app

### read the field ownership table
GET {{base}}/v1/resources/app/owners

### read the auditable history
GET {{base}}/v1/resources/app/history?limit=20
